 "remarks": "Welcome to one of Ledgebrook's most distinctive homes-a rare detached 1960 single-family residence tucked into a private, wooded setting within one of Norwalk's most established condominium communities. Full of character, warmth, and a touch of retro charm, the home begins with an inviting front porch and continues inside with hardwood floors, a wood-burning fireplace, sun-filled living spaces, and two cozy bedrooms surrounded by mature trees. A bright private office provides an ideal work-from-home space, while the recently renovated bathroom thoughtfully retains the home's vintage-inspired feel. Downstairs, the walkout lower level adds approximately 660 square feet of valuable additional space, including a family room and laundry area with new luxury vinyl plank flooring. An additional unfinished area-the home's original garage, complete with its original garage door-offers tremendous flexibility for storage, a workshop, hobby space, gym, or future possibilities. Adding to the home's unusual appeal is the privacy and independence of a detached residence combined with access to Ledgebrook's extensive amenities. The property also includes deeded underground garage parking spaces on a separate deed.",
